1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Hey! Youpi!

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
-[Menthuthuyoupi] Hmm?
-[Shoot gasps]

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
[Knuckle] Over here, you bastard!

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Works for me.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,000
That'll distract Youpi,

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,000
and, if we're lucky,

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:34,000
it might even
be enough to save Shoot.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
[opening theme music playing]

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

11
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
[singer singing in English]

12
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

13
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
[singer singing in English]

14
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
DUTY X AND X QUESTION

16
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:18,000
that the name he had spoken
with such confidence

17
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
had aroused Welfin
and Bloster's suspicions

18
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
as he headed
deep beneath the palace

19
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,000
to continue his search for Palm.

20
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
[elevator dings]

21
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
that he would not leave
the palace without finding her.

22
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
[Ikalgo] Palm is a friend
of my friends,

23
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
and I will rescue her.

24
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Any friend of theirs
is a friend of mine!

25
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
[dramatic music playing]

26
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:29,000
[narrator] The very fact
that Palm was risking her life

27
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
because I decided that I would.

28
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:07,000
it would automatically go back up.

29
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
To ascend from the basement,

30
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,000
only one person at a time
could use the elevator,

31
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
and on top of that,

32
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
a specific code had to be entered.

33
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
an alarm would sound,
and the doors would lock.

34
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
-Entering the wrong code three times…
-[elevator dings]

35
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
would alert security
and release sleeping gas.

36
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
The violator would then be captured.

37
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
In other words,
an error meant death.

38
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
[panel buzzes]

39
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,000
[narrator] Both the violator

40
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
and the code's original owner
would be killed,

41
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:08,000
making one's personal entry code
as valuable as one's own life.

42
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,000
The only people whose codes

43
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
allow them to use the elevator
without these restrictions

44
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
And it was easier
to use this elevator

45
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
than the freight entrance,

46
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
[elevator dings]

47
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,000
[Welfin] What is that smell?

48
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,000
What's wrong with Flutter?

49
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Yeah, that's Blo, all right.

50
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,000
I can tell by the scent.

51
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
but it's faint.

52
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:15,000
[narrator] The stench
of Flutter's decomposing body

53
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,000
dulled Welfin's sense of smell.

54
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,000
[Welfin] Blo followed Flutter

55
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:24,000
when he went underground,
so when Flutter said, "Hagya,"

56
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
there's no way he didn't notice it.

57
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Unless Bloster's in on it, too.

58
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
I was keeping a close eye
on the intruder,

59
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:51,000
If he was and if he's working
with the intruder,

60
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
-[gasps]
-[gunfire]

61
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
So he could ambush me downstairs!

62
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Damn it!

63
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,000
[panting]

64
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Damn it. This is my chance.

65
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Flutter is clearly acting suspiciously.

66
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:20,000
If I can just set him up
as the perp of the bomb threat,

67
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:25,000
I can prove to Bizeff
how valuable I am.

68
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Bizeff!

69
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Forget Flutter.

70
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
First, I need to find Bizeff.

71
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:12,000
If you'll both excuse me,
my job here is done.

72
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Killua, when you get inside,

73
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,000
you make the call.

74
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
"Make the call"?

75
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
and disappeared into the darkness.

76
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[suspenseful music playing]

77
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Meleoron and Shoot
could only hold their breaths

78
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
and brace for what would come.

79
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
Bring it on!

80
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,000
I get it now.

81
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,000
So this thing is yours, huh?

82
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
It is time now.

83
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
You have accrued interest.

84
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Hmm?

85
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
So the number went up, did it?

86
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
[suspenseful music playing]

87
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
[grunts]

88
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
[growls]

89
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
[gasps]

90
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:19,000
I guess my attacks
don't affect it at all.

91
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
What is that damn thing?

92
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[chuckles]

93
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Don't run away!

94
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Answer me! What is this?

95
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:37,000
You really think I'd tell you,
you son of a bitch!

96
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
If you wanna know,
you gotta catch me!

97
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,000
[Meleoron] Damn!

98
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Knuckle's planning
to fight Youpi alone,

99
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
and I can't get to him,

100
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:01,000
not through that deadly,
sword-like onslaught.

101
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
There's no way!

102
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[groans]

103
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
If I do,

104
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:52,000
then Hotel Rafflesia
will cease to function.

105
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Any minor wound, any injury…

106
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
will surely not be in vain.

107
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
keep going.

108
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:46,000
[Meleoron] I can't…

109
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
say it!

110
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:53,000
I can't tell Shoot to give his all,
'cause he already is.

111
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
no matter how much I want to.

112
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,000
Come on, Shoot!
You have to survive!

113
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Please don't die!

114
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
No one's here.

115
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Don't panic.

116
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Look around carefully.

117
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:57,000
If I'm found out, I could
still pass as one of the ants.

118
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Except,
depending on who I run into,

119
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Okay, activate.

120
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:35,000
There, that's Morel's Smoky Jail,

121
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:38,000
which means that Morel and Pouf

122
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
are facing off one-on-one
in the throne room.

123
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
That only leaves two,

124
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Gon and Killua.

125
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,000
[gasps]

126
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:06,000
[tense music playing]

127
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Welfin?

128
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Oh, no! He's trouble!

129
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Out of all the Squadron Leaders,
he's the biggest skeptic.

130
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Once he suspects you,

131
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
he won't trust you again
till you're dead!

132
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:25,000
[Welfin sniffing]

133
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Which way do I go?

134
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
[continues sniffing]

135
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
What if he goes the same way?

136
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
What if I can't hold
my breath that long?

137
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,000
I'm at my limit!

138
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
[groans]

139
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
I gotta exhale and inhale
in one fast move.

140
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,000
[exhales]

141
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Huh?

142
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:23,000
[Meleoron]
And now inhale. Activate!

143
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[gasping]

144
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
An enemy?

145
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,000
[narrator] Welfin's ability
reflected his guarded,

146
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
I'm gonna count to three.
You better show yourself.

147
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:08,000
And if you don't,
I'll tear you to pieces!

148
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
[growls]

149
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,000
One…

150
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,000
two…

151
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
three!

152
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,000
[powering up]

153
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:47,000
[narrator] To use Missileman,
Welfin chooses his target.

154
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Had Meleoron
stayed in the same place,

155
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Welfin's attack would certainly
have reached its target,

156
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
whether Welfin
could sense him or not.

157
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,000
But because the criteria
were not met, it misfired.

158
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Once activated,
Missileman will pursue its target

159
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
until it hits its mark.

160
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:26,000
No one can sustain the impact
and survive.

161
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,000
He was even suspicious
of his own ability.

162
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
He only thought
of Missileman as a tool

163
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
to give him leverage in negotiations.

164
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
would have more worries
than he could tolerate.

165
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:15,000
Someone was here. I'm sure of it.

166
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:23,000
The fact that they're using
that kind of deodorant

167
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
proves that they know
about my nose.

168
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
That means there are traitors
among us.

169
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,000
There's no doubt about it.

170
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
So there are others besides Flutter?

171
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
There would almost have to be.

172
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,000
What's more,
it's gotta be someone I know.

173
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
That's why they're hiding their scent.

174
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
'Cause they can kill me
whenever they want?

175
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
really the right thing to do?

176
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:39,000
[triumph music playing]

177
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Gon and Killua
had finally found their target,

178
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:18,000
a Royal Guard by the name of Neferpitou,

179
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
and continued their quest to avenge Kite.

180
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
[closing theme music playing]

181
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,000
[Gon] Killua.

182
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:43,000
[both] No matter what, don't lose hope!

183
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
